<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konrad I of Oleśnica</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1294–1366</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konrad I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olesnica">Oleśnica</a> was a Silesian Piast duke, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-glogow">Henry III of Głogów</a>. In the division of his father's lands he received Oleśnica, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Wrocław</a>, and founded the Duchy of Oleśnica, which he ruled until 1366. In 1329 he accepted the overlordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, like most Silesian dukes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-olesnica.jpg" alt="Konrad I of Oleśnica" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konrad_I_Ole%C5%9Bnicki.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
